+// pages in the row.  The normal case7 producer and reducer never instantiate
+// this direct BF16 conversion/store path; they are only guarded away for the
+// same device-side length predicate in their case7 dispatches.
+//
+// This is deliberately a separate kernel rather than a DIRECT_OUT template
+// mode on the split producer.  It preserves the normal case7 three-split
+// producer geometry for rows with full_pages > 43 and gives short rows a
+// complete, independent owner.  The fixed <true,false> QK/PV helpers are the
+// already-validated case7 head-pair/z8 calculation body.
